      "problem": "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5})=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{5})^{-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}+(\\sqrt{5})^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\sqrt{5}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
